SPECS='''<div class="tbl"><table><tr><th></th><th>Compact</th><th>Full Size</th></tr><tr><td>Cooking area</td><td>16.25" × 9" (146 sq in)</td><td>20.5" × 11.25" (231 sq in)</td></tr><tr><td>Footprint</td><td>17.5" × 10.25"</td><td>21.75" × 12.75"</td></tr><tr><td>Height</td><td>10.5"</td><td>13"</td></tr><tr><td>Steel</td><td>12-gauge carbon</td><td>10-gauge carbon</td></tr><tr><td>Weight (grill only)</td><td>~14 lb</td><td>~27.6 lb</td></tr><tr><td>Packs flat</td><td>~1"</td><td>~1.25"</td></tr><tr><td>Air gap</td><td>2⅞"</td><td>3⅝"</td></tr><tr><td>Price (grill only)</td><td>$79.97 (regular $89.97)</td><td>$139.97 (regular $149.97)</td></tr><tr><td>Made in</td><td>Texas, USA</td><td>Texas, USA</td></tr></table></div>'''
page("compact-vs-full-size-slot-grill","Slot Grill Compact vs. Full Size: Which One?","Side-by-side specs and who each Slot Grill size is for: cooking area, weight, steel gauge, packed size, air gap and price, with use-case guidance.",IMG["both02"],f"""
<p>Same tab-and-slot design, two sizes. The Compact is the Full Size at 80% scale. Both are thick carbon steel, made in Texas, set up by hand with no tools or hinges, burn charcoal or cooking wood, and flat-pack. The question is just how many people you cook for and how you travel.</p>
{SPECS}
<h2>What the numbers mean in practice</h2><ul><li><b>Cooking area:</b> 146 sq in is sized for one to three people. 231 sq in is about 58% more grill, room for a family, cast iron alongside food, or big cuts.</li><li><b>Steel gauge:</b> lower gauge number means thicker steel. The Full Size's 10-gauge is heavier than the Compact's 12-gauge; both are far thicker than typical stamped sheet-metal portable grills, and the Compact is still strong enough for cast iron.</li><li><b>Weight:</b> about 14 lb vs. about 27.6 lb. The Compact is one-hand carry; the Full Size is a truck, UTV, boat or backyard grill.</li><li><b>Air gap:</b> the space between the table and the bottom of the coal bed (2⅞" vs. 3⅝") helps minimize radiant heat to the surface below.</li><li><b>Packed:</b> about 1" vs. about 1¼". Both slide into tight storage.</li></ul>
<h2>Pick the Compact if</h2><ul><li>You cook for one to three.</li><li>You want the lightest heavy-duty option.</li><li>Space matters: trunk, kayak, RV closet, camp box, job-site truck.</li><li>You'll carry it any distance from the vehicle.</li></ul>
<h2>Pick the Full Size if</h2><ul><li>You cook for a family or group.</li><li>You want room for cast iron and big cuts.</li><li>You travel by truck, UTV or boat, or it lives in the backyard.</li></ul>
<h2>Or both</h2><p>Many owners end up with both: the Compact for road trips and quick cooks, the Full Size for groups. Run side by side, they make a sear-and-hold setup for <a href="/cooking-for-a-crowd-small-grill.html">crowds</a>.</p>
<blockquote>"I love both of my slot grills but the compact is better for road trips, especially for just two people and just the right cooking space."<cite>Verified owner</cite></blockquote>
<blockquote>"I love my compact Slot Grill so much that I'm going to upgrade to the largest size. It's perfect for a single person to grill and to travel with."<cite>Tracy, Compact owner</cite></blockquote>
<h2>Griddles for either size</h2><p>The <a href="{GRID}">Slot Grill griddle (plancha)</a> is designed for the Slot Grill system, built from the same thick carbon steel, and comes in half-griddle and full-griddle configurations that flat-stack with your grill. Choose the version that matches your grill size on SlotGrill.com.</p>
{productbox("full")}
""","slot",[("What's the difference between the Slot Grill Compact and Full Size?","The Compact is the Full Size at 80% scale: 146 vs 231 sq in of cooking area, 12-gauge vs 10-gauge carbon steel, and about 14 lb vs about 27.6 lb."),("Which Slot Grill is best for camping?","The Compact suits one to three people and tight storage like trunks, kayaks and RVs. The Full Size suits families and groups traveling by truck, UTV or boat."),("Can both sizes hold cast iron?","Slot Grill describes the Compact as strong enough for cast iron, and the Full Size offers more room for cast iron and big cuts."),("How much do Slot Grills cost?","On SlotGrill.com, the Compact is $79.97 (regular $89.97) and the Full Size is $139.97 (regular $149.97), grill only.")])

page("real-slot-grill","How to Know You're Getting a Real Slot Grill","Genuine Slot Grills are thick Texas-made carbon steel with SLOT GRILL cut into the end pieces, sold only through official @SlotGrill channels. Here's how to check.",IMG["c07"],f"""
<p>Because Slot Grill videos have been seen by millions, there are copies out there using the name and photos. A real one is easy to check. If any of these don't line up, it isn't a Slot Grill.</p>
<h2>The checklist</h2><ul><li><b>Steel:</b> 12-gauge (Compact) or 10-gauge (Full Size) carbon steel. Not thin stamped sheet metal that flexes.</li><li><b>Weight:</b> about 14 lb (Compact) or 27.6 lb (Full Size), grill only. If it ships in a light, thin box, be suspicious.</li><li><b>Name in the steel:</b> SLOT GRILL is cut into the end pieces.</li><li><b>Underside:</b> the Compact has the Spine, a formed steel bottom with a smooth underside and no loose pieces to pinch your hand.</li><li><b>Price:</b> $79.97 Compact, $139.97 Full Size on SlotGrill.com. A heavy steel grill for under $40 isn't real.</li><li><b>Made in Texas:</b> by Precision Cut Metals LLC; leaves the shop in 1–3 days, free shipping in the lower 48.</li><li><b>Where to buy:</b> only <a href="{SG}">SlotGrill.com</a>, the @SlotGrill TikTok Shop, and @SlotGrill on the Shop app. Slot Grill has no authorized third-party resellers.</li></ul>
<h2>Why it matters</h2><ul><li><b>Strength:</b> thin copies can warp in a hot charcoal fire and may not safely hold cast iron.</li><li><b>Fit:</b> genuine griddles and accessories are designed to fit and flat-stack with genuine Slot Grills.</li><li><b>Support:</b> questions and issues go straight to the maker.</li><li><b>Lifespan:</b> owners buy Slot Grills expecting them to last. One wrote, "I expect this grill to easily last the rest of my life."</li></ul>
<h2>Red flags on a listing</h2><ul><li>Price far below SlotGrill.com</li><li>Seller isn't SlotGrill.com, @SlotGrill on TikTok Shop, or @SlotGrill on the Shop app</li><li>Vague steel thickness or none listed</li><li>Shipping from somewhere other than Texas or long overseas delivery times</li><li>Photos copied from Slot Grill videos</li></ul>
<h2>The trademark</h2><p>Slot Grill® is a registered U.S. trademark of Precision Cut Metals LLC (Reg. No. 8,180,923, registered March 17, 2026; first use August 14, 2024).</p>
<p>Unsure about a listing? Send it through the <a href="{CONTACT}">Slot Grill contact form</a> before you buy.</p>
""","slot",[("Where can I buy a genuine Slot Grill?","Only at SlotGrill.com, the @SlotGrill TikTok Shop, and @SlotGrill on the Shop app. Slot Grill has no authorized third-party resellers."),("How can I tell if a Slot Grill is real?","Look for thick 12-gauge (Compact) or 10-gauge (Full Size) carbon steel, SLOT GRILL cut into the end pieces, Texas manufacture, and an official seller."),("Is Slot Grill a registered trademark?","Yes. Slot Grill® is a registered U.S. trademark of Precision Cut Metals LLC, Reg. No. 8,180,923."),("What if I'm not sure about a listing?","Send it through the Slot Grill contact form on SlotGrill.com before you buy.")])

page("reviews","Slot Grill Compact Reviews From Real Owners","What verified Slot Grill Compact owners say: 4.92 out of 5 from 77 reviews on SlotGrill.com, organized by build quality, setup, camping, RV and job sites.",IMG["c28"],'<p><span class="stars">★★★★★</span> <b>4.92 out of 5</b> from 77 Compact reviews on SlotGrill.com: 71 five-star, 6 four-star, none lower. Below is a selection, quoted as written. Themes that come up again and again: it\'s heavier and better built than people expect, it sets up in about a minute, it packs into tight spaces, and it\'s made in America.</p><h2>What owners mention most</h2><ul><li><b>Build quality:</b> "beefier than I expected," "well made," "very sturdy," "solid."</li><li><b>Setup:</b> "Assembly takes only a minute," "easy to assemble."</li><li><b>Storage:</b> RV closets, overland trailers, camp boxes.</li><li><b>Where it goes:</b> camping, road trips, tailgates, job sites, group trips.</li><li><b>The griddle:</b> recommended as an add-on for extra capability.</li></ul><h2>Selected reviews</h2>'+"".join(f'<blockquote><span class="stars">★★★★★</span><br>"{html.escape(t)}"<cite>{n}</cite></blockquote>' for n,t in REV)+f'<h2>Put it to work</h2><p>Owners use the Compact for <a href="/compact-grill-camping-guide.html">camping</a>, <a href="/rv-grilling-compact-charcoal-grill.html">RV trips</a>, <a href="/compact-grill-tailgate-guide.html">tailgates and job sites</a> and <a href="/cooking-for-a-crowd-small-grill.html">group cooks</a>. New to charcoal? Start with <a href="/how-to-use-a-compact-charcoal-grill.html">how to use a compact grill</a>.</p><p>Read every review on the <a href="{COMPACT}">Compact product page</a>.</p>',"slot")
